    {
     "id": "clm_canopy_fractions_veg_step1_p48",
     "description": "Vegetated canopy-fraction pin against clm_canopyflux.csv (flx stage, step 1, patch 48, column 47): a vegetated patch (frac_veg_nosno = 1, elai = 2.40369491489884357, esai = 3.87127514466065858e-01) holding liqcan = 8.03777473957576621e-02 mm at the end of the step. The flx stage dumps after the CanopyFluxes evaporation update (CanopyFluxesMod.F90:1618-1631), so the dumped liqcan is the post-evap state while the canopy fractions were computed by this step's hydrology from the pre-evap storage — the pin is exact anyway because the fwet clamp saturates: evaluated at the dumped state, the raw law (h2ocan/(vegt*liq_canopy_storage_scalar))^0.666666666666 (BulkDiag_FracWet, CanopyHydrologyMod.F90:1170) gives 0.4361, above maximum_leaf_wetted_fraction = 0.05, so fwet = 0.05 exactly as dumped (:1171; 85 of the 192 flx rows saturate even at post-evap storage, while the 10 rows with fwet < 0.05 are unpinnable — their pre-evap storage is not dumped). Pins the vegetated branch of the fraction laws at nonzero canopy storage: the fwet clamp, fdry = (1-fwet)*elai/(elai+esai) (:1182) = 8.18221232969503554e-01, fcansno = 0 (snocan = 0, :1176), and the storage intermediates h2ocan = liqcan + snocan (:1166), vegt = frac_veg_nosno*(elai+esai) (:1169), liqcanmx = liq_canopy_storage_scalar*(elai+esai) (CanopyHydrologyMod.F90:755), snocanmx = snow_canopy_storage_scalar*(elai+esai) (:757), whose expected values are f64 evaluations of those equations at the dumped elai/esai/liqcan/snocan. The storage state is set via initial_conditions with time_span {0,0} (MOSART precedent for ODE-state unknowns) because the evaporation that produced the post-evap liqcan is outside CanopyHydrology. Not pinned here: the interception/throughfall flux split (fpiliq/fpisnow/qflx_intercepted_*/qflx_through_* are NaN at the flx stage — the hyd stage, which dumps them, traces only the bare patches 1-16), the excess-fall fluxes, and qflx_liq_grnd (a wtcol-weighted column aggregate for these vegetated columns).",
