     "description": "Ice-branch saturation humidity law against clm_qsat.csv row 191 (the coldest traced QSat call, T = 242.24520844746371 K = the dump's T minimum, p = 68444.8972021591617 Pa): qsatg_snow = qsat_qs(T,p) (QSatMod.F90:90-103, ice polynomial c0..c8 scaled by 100 to Pa and 0.622*es/(p-0.378*es); the power-sum poly8 form agrees with the Fortran's Horner form to round-off) reproduces the dumped qs = 3.14386008144803511e-4 kg/kg. Also pins the qg_snow = qsatg_snow branch for snl < 0 (SurfaceHumidityMod.F90:194-196). The dump's qsdT/esdT columns are identically 0 (the traced callers do not request derivatives; the derivative law is pinned through dqgdT by the clm_qsat_snow_surfhum_* tests instead). All 192 qsat rows are at T < 273.15 K, so the liquid branch (td >= 0) of qsat_esat/qsat_esat_dT is untested — see stage2/README-clm.md.",
