     "id": "clm_soilfluxes_soil_qsat_step1_c1",
     "description": "Soil-branch QSat wiring against clm_soilfluxes.csv (step 1, column 1) with the post-solve top-soil temperature t_soisno_1 = 225.739712678586642 K (the soilfluxes dump's t_soisno_1, which equals the soiltemp exit-stage j = 1 row to round-off on all 192 rows — the W2 fix makes t_soisno_1..3 real) and forc_pbot = 68134.1361002605699 Pa from clm_bareground.csv (step 1, column 1): qsatg_soil_raw = qsat_qs(T,p) and qsatgdT_soil = qsat_qsdT(T,p) (SurfaceHumidityMod.F90:185-190) reproduce the raw QSat law at the soil temperature. The supersaturated-window clamp (qsatg > forc_q > hr*qsatg, :185-190) is inactive here — qsatg_soil = 4.93e-5 kg/kg lies below forc_q = 6.48e-4 kg/kg (clm_bareground.csv step 1 column 1) — so qsatg_soil = qsatg_soil_raw and qsatgdT_soil stays nonzero, pinning the unclamped soil branch of the qsatg_soil/qsatgdT_soil wiring. qg_soil = hr*qsatg_soil is not pinned: hr needs the top-layer soil water parameters (h2osoi_liq/h2osoi_ice, dz, watsat, sucsat, bsw), which are not dumped.",
