    {
     "id": "clm_htvp_sublimation",
     "description": "Latent heat of sublimation against clm_run_imports.csv (preflux stage: htvp = 2.8347e6 J/kg exactly on all 192 rows) and clm_soilfluxes.csv (eflx_lh_grnd/qflx_evap_soi = 2,834,700 exactly on all 192 rows, SoilFluxesMod.F90:394): the top layer is frozen with no liquid water (the traced columns carry h2osoi_liq = 0 and h2osoi_ice = 5.39439117719703098 kg/m2 in the top snow layer, the soiltemp entry j = -8 value for column 1 step 1), so the htvp branch condition h2osoi_liq <= 0 and h2osoi_ice > 0 (BiogeophysPreFluxCalcsMod.F90:354-358) selects hsub = LATICE + LATVAP = 3.337e5 + 2.501e6 = 2.8347e6 J/kg (SHR_CONST_LATSUB, not the 2.835e6 icepack-style rounded value).",
